hi I'm Chelsea chupp product manager for  AIML and HPC  thanks for joining me today as we review  Google Cloud's HPC toolkit  let's get started  [Music]  at Google we've recognized that the hvc  community uses a wide array of  Technologies including offerings from  partners and custom in-house Solutions  setting up iterating upon configurations  and tearing down these clusters can be  quite challenging  it can also be difficult to effectively  combine all these Technologies  especially if the cloud is an unfamiliar  environment our mission for the cloud  HPC toolkit is to make it easy for our  users to deploy repeatable HPC  environments which are optimized for HPC  workloads based on Google Cloud's proven  best practices  the toolkit provides a simplified  experience for first-time cloud and  terraform users while maintaining the  ability to configure and customize your  cluster for your specific needs  the toolkit is a free and open source  tool so you only need to pay for the  resources that are provisioned let's  talk about what is in the HPC toolkit  the HBC toolkit consists of a set of  blueprints which Define the HPC cluster  or system and calls a set of modules  which is used to deploy actual Cloud  infrastructure such as compute  networking and storage resources  one way to think of it is that blueprint  calls the modules to be able to create  the infrastructure that you need in the  modules we support schedulers such as  slurm HD Condor and Google Cloud batch  with more partner offerings to come  for storage we support file store Intel  daus ddn exascaler luster and local SSD  and persistent disk  other modules support key  functionalities such as SPAC Dell Omnia  and Cloud monitoring  for a complete list visit the hvc  toolkit GitHub repo  you can also extend the toolkit's  functionality by using the modules  authored outside of the toolkit either  from a git repository or a local  directory  the HPC toolkit modules are the building  blocks used to define your HPC  environment these modules Define  high-level components such as parallel  file systems workload managers and  software stacks and networking  infrastructure  the HBC toolkit comes pre-packaged with  a growing list of core and owned  Community modules  these modules are designed to work  together to make it easy to combine  partner Technology Solutions with and on  your Google Cloud infrastructure  now let's talk about the blueprints  the blueprint is your design plan  referencing a list of modules and how  they're all interconnected  a blueprint is the only part that you  need to understand to deploy your HPC  cluster  it's a simple text configuration file or  a yaml file that composes your entire  HPC environment including the  infrastructure and software  the hvc toolkit provides a set of  supported and tested standard blueprints  you can use These Blueprints as is or  customize them based upon your specific  use case and requirements  to actually run the HPC toolkit we use  ghpc engine to convert a blueprint to a  deployment folder which can then be  deployed onto Google Cloud  once deployed you can then easily add on  monitoring and analytics to know exactly  how your cluster or system is performing  the deployment folder will contain all  of the underlying terraform Packer and  scripts needed to deploy a complete hvc  environment that has been wired together  as described by your blueprint  it can be tracked as source code and  distributed the blueprint of the HPC  toolkit describes a complex environment  in just a simple text or yaml file  by only having to modify the yaml file  it saves you having to Wade through  thousands of lines of code to make  changes or modifications  and only a few line the blueprint file  will generate the necessary scripts and  modules to create your fully functioning  HPC environment the hvc toolkit creates  standard repeatable deployment templates  saving your team time to achieve Optimal  Performance  it also eases the learning curve if your  team is new to Cloud  as a free open source tool extensibility  is a key design principle to enable the  technologies that you require  we look forward to working with you and  hearing of your success thanks for  listening check out our other videos or  cloud.google.com  hpc-toolkit to learn more  [Music]  foreign
 

